---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout>

  <section class="hero">

    <div class="patent-banner">
      ✅ Provisional Patent Application Filed
    </div>

    <img
      src="/SVG-DBR-LOGO.png"
      alt="Dual Brain Robotics Logo"
      class="hero-logo"
    />

    <h1>Dual Brain Robotics</h1>

    <h2>Artificial Intelligence Inspired by the Human Brain</h2>

    <p class="hero-text">
      Developed by Dr. Alexander Durig, Dual Brain Robotics introduces
      a bilateral cognitive architecture inspired by the cooperative
      processing systems of the human brain.
    </p>

    <p class="hero-text">
      Rather than relying on a single monolithic intelligence,
      the architecture explores how two complementary cognitive
      systems can interact to produce more adaptive, context-aware,
      and human-compatible artificial intelligence.
    </p>

    <div class="patent-status">
      U.S. Utility-Provisional Patent Application<br />
      Dual Brain Robotics Architecture<br />
      Application No. 64/181,346
    </div>

    <div class="hero-buttons">
      <a href="/architecture" class="button">
        Explore the Architecture
      </a>

      <a href="/patent" class="button secondary">
        Patent Overview
      </a>

      <a href="/research-foundation" class="button secondary">
        Research Foundation
      </a>
    </div>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Two Minds. One Intelligence.</h2>

    <p>
      Most AI systems are built around a single cognitive engine.
      Dual Brain Robotics proposes a fundamentally different approach:
      two specialized systems working together through continuous
      communication and integration.
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>The Architecture</h2>

    <div class="architecture-grid">

      <div class="architecture-card">
        <h3>Logical Intelligence</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Planning</li>
          <li>Sequencing</li>
          <li>Language</li>
          <li>Analytical Reasoning</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="architecture-card">
        <h3>Integration Layer</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Coordination</li>
          <li>Consensus Building</li>
          <li>Conflict Resolution</li>
          <li>Self-Modeling</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="architecture-card">
        <h3>Perceptual Intelligence</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Pattern Recognition</li>
          <li>Context Awareness</li>
          <li>Creativity</li>
          <li>Social Understanding</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Why It Matters</h2>

    <p>
      Human intelligence emerges from interaction between specialized
      regions of the brain. Dual Brain Robotics applies this insight
      to artificial intelligence and robotics.
    </p>

    <p>
      By separating complementary forms of cognition and allowing them
      to cooperate, the architecture seeks to improve adaptability,
      contextual understanding, decision quality, and human interaction.
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Research Foundation</h2>

    <p>
      The Dual Brain Robotics Architecture is the culmination of decades
      of work in social psychology, perception theory, autism research,
      qualitative models, and the study of consciousness.
    </p>

    <p>
      These disciplines collectively provide the conceptual foundation
      for a new generation of artificial cognitive architectures.
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Potential Applications</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Autonomous Robotics</li>
      <li>Human-Robot Interaction</li>
      <li>Adaptive Learning Systems</li>
      <li>Assistive Technologies</li>
      <li>Cognitive Architecture Research</li>
      <li>Consciousness Studies</li>
    </ul>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>The Beginning of a New Exploration</h2>

    <p>
      The Dual Brain Robotics Architecture represents an effort to bridge
      neuroscience, psychology, consciousness theory, and artificial
      intelligence.
    </p>

    <p>
      Research, development, and prototyping are actively underway as the
      project moves from theory toward implementation.
    </p>

  </section>

</MainLayout>
